---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>The Student Portal is the React-based workspace for enrolled students. Your school controls which areas are enabled, so some features described here may not appear on your account.</p>\n<h2>Dashboard</h2>\n<p>After signing in, the dashboard shows your current enrollment status, upcoming classes, announcements, and shortcuts to the areas you use most. First-time users see a short onboarding checklist that can be dismissed once completed.</p>\n<h2>Classes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Open a class to see <strong>posts and materials</strong> from your teacher.</li>\n<li>Submit <strong>assignment submissions</strong> directly from the class page before the deadline.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Schedule</h2>\n<p>The schedule page shows your weekly class timetable for the active semester. Printable timetable PDFs can be downloaded when your school enables them.</p>\n<h2>Tuition and statements of account</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The <strong>tuition</strong> area shows your current assessment and payment status.</li>\n<li><strong>Statements of account (SOA)</strong> issued by the cashier appear here with download links. Each SOA carries a signed verification link so third parties (such as sponsors or employers) can confirm it is genuine.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Digital ID card</h2>\n<p>Your <strong>digital ID card</strong> shows your student photo, identifier, and a QR code. Staff and verification kiosks can scan the code to confirm your enrollment status through the public verification page — no account needed for verification.</p>\n<h2>Announcements and notifications</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Announcements</strong> from the school appear on your dashboard and in the announcements page.</li>\n<li>The <strong>Notification Center</strong> collects messages sent to you — enrollment updates, grade releases, payment notices, class suspensions, school events, and reminders.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Help and support</h2>\n<p>If something is wrong with a record or you cannot access a feature, open a <strong>help ticket</strong> from the portal instead of sharing your account. Staff responses appear in the same thread.</p>\n<h2>Profile and security</h2>\n<p>From profile settings you can update your information (where permitted), enable <strong>two-factor authentication</strong>, register <strong>passkeys</strong>, and manage personal <strong>API keys</strong> when your school allows them.</p>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-tip">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">Keep your account private</p><p>School staff will never ask for your password. Use two-factor authentication and report suspicious sign-in prompts through a help ticket.</p>\n</div>'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Student Portal"
  path="/docs/user-guide/student-portal"
  description="What students can do in the KoAkademy student portal — classes, schedule, tuition, digital ID, and notifications."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
